SUMMARY:NC Arboretum Walk: Gardens\, Trails\, a Stream\, & a Plant Sale
DESCRIPTION:Haywood County Walking Meetup Group\nWe will be joining the As
 heville Amblers\, AARP\, and perhaps some others for this walk. The walk i
 s free\, although the Amblers do accept donations (suggested donation: $4.
 00).\n\nMeet to register inside the Baker Visitor Center at 08:30 a.m. Res
 trooms are available at the start point. Step-off is at 9:00 a.m.\n\nThe w
 alk includes both a guided 5 KM and guided 10 KM option. Both walks have s
 ome moderate hills and stair climbing. A significant part of the route is 
 on well-groomed trails with very few obstacles. There are some hills and n
 atural surface paths. Some people will want walking poles.\n\nWalks are th
 rough picturesque formal gardens\, the Bonsai Exhibition\, shaded scenic t
 rails\, and paths along a swift flowing stream. The trees should be just s
 tarting to color for fall.\n\nAfter the walk\, enjoy the annual plant show
  and sale.\n\nDress for the weather\; consider a hat and sunscreen. Sneake
 rs should be fine\, unless it has rained recently. Be sure to bring plenty
  of water and a protein snack.\n\nDogs on leash are welcome but are not al
 lowed in buildings or in the Bonsai Exhibition. Trail strollers should be 
 ok.\n\nThe NC Arboretum does not have an admission fee\, but they charge $
 25 per car parking fee (so pack as many people in your car as you can). We
  recommend for the driver to purchase the lowest level annual membership w
 hich includes free parking. (Of course\, you may want a higher-level membe
 rship\, your choice.) We walk at the Arboretum at least six times per year
 .
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/haywood-county-walking-meetup-group/e
 vents/316656217/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260921T211143Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260921T211143Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
